TEST 38099 -- MRP ring switch over with 500ms recovery time
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22, tb470

VERDICT: UNMEASURED -- no MRP-capable ring partners exist on this bench.

Every case in this group needs a three-node MRP ring ("Configure sw1 with the
MRP MRC config", "Configure sw2 with the MRP MRC config"). The three bench
devices ARE cabled as a ring, so the topology is right, but neither partner can
run MRP at all:

  device                 show mrp / show mrp ring   config 'mrp ?'      licence
  IE520 stack (DUT)      supported                  ring  Configure...  MRP: YES
  AR4050S-5G             % Invalid input            % Unrecognized      MRP listed
  x230-10GP (AW+ 5.5.5)  % Invalid input            % Unrecognized      no MRP

Checked in BOTH exec and configure mode on each device, so this is not a mode
or PATH artefact.

The DUT side is not what blocks this -- it carries the full command set
('mrp ring' in config, 'show mrp ports|ring' in exec) and MRP is licensed. A
ring could be configured on it today; it would simply have no peers, and
'show mrp ring' would never report operational, which is the first thing every
one of these cases checks.

Observation for review: the AR4050S LISTS MRP as a licensed feature while
exposing no MRP CLI whatsoever. A licence entry is not a capability.

TO UNBLOCK: two MRP-capable AlliedWare Plus switches as ring partners. The
existing cabling already forms the ring, so only the devices need swapping.

Full detail and the capability matrix: README.md in this directory.
